WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.037
Meet Agents Foundry, the organizational layer for AI. Give AI employees a

00:00:05.037 --> 00:00:09.288
role, a team, and a clear boundary, with people in charge.

00:00:10.288 --> 00:00:14.727
The guided onboarding target is five to ten minutes, once your organization

00:00:14.727 --> 00:00:18.796
and employee accounts are configured. Here is the QA assignment flow.

00:00:19.796 --> 00:00:24.279
Start in your organization's admin workspace. Choose the QA Engineer blueprint and

00:00:24.279 --> 00:00:27.269
the active employees who will receive an agent.

00:00:28.269 --> 00:00:33.899
Name the agent and complete the blueprint questionnaire. Define its project scope,

00:00:33.899 --> 00:00:39.061
working environment, and configuration preferences. Review the enforced capabilities before assigning.

00:00:40.061 --> 00:00:45.307
Create and assign. Up to twenty-five active employees can receive distinct agent

00:00:45.307 --> 00:00:50.554
instances from one setup. Each gets an employee-bound, signed assignment and separate

00:00:50.554 --> 00:00:51.428
conversation history.

00:00:52.428 --> 00:00:56.696
Employees open Your assigned agents and verify the agent before selecting it.

00:00:56.696 --> 00:01:00.963
The workspace checks the signature and ownership, connecting the role to the

00:01:00.963 --> 00:01:02.386
right person and organization.

00:01:03.386 --> 00:01:08.404
The QA employee supports planning. Browser execution requires human approval, and production

00:01:08.404 --> 00:01:13.423
deployment is denied. An approved run is ready for the next step;

00:01:13.423 --> 00:01:15.932
connected execution remains on the roadmap.

00:01:16.932 --> 00:01:22.202
Start with the QA foundation. Explore fifty-five specialist role concepts and the

00:01:22.202 --> 00:01:27.471
wider workforce vision. Build your AI workforce. Run it like a real

00:01:27.471 --> 00:01:27.910
organization.
